edAt":"2026-09-24T11:13:11Z","mergeCommit":{"oid":"6ad8b9877f1c6280f7d424c5b890ab576eb8a4ad"},"closingIssuesReferences":{"nodes":[{"number":10799},{"number":10800}]}},"n10800":{"__typename":"Issue","number":10800,"title":"[review] [Reviewer (chatgpt-codex-connector[bot])] Feedback on src/engines/physics_engines/pendul...","state":"CLOSED","body":"## Review Comment from Reviewer (chatgpt-codex-connector[bot])\n\n**Source PR:** #10798 - fix(tour_baselines): reconstruct presets from verified arrays and keep pendulum packages qualifiable\n**File:** `src/engines/physics_engines/pendulum/python/motion_matching/qualification.py` (line 307)\n**Original Comment:** https://github.com/D-sorganization/UpstreamDrift/pull/10798#discussion_r4090113714\n\n---\n\n### Feedback\n\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Hash the actual pendulum inertia parameters**\n\nThe baseline contract defines `fixed_inertia_hash` as the digest of segment masses and rotational inertias, but this value contains only the model label and link lengths—the same geometric inputs already covered by `fixed_geometry_hash`. If the default arm/shaft/club masses, center-of-mass ratios, or inertias used by `create_calibrated_double_pendulum_dynamics()` change, the hash remains identical and a replay can be treated as using the recorded physics when it does not. Build this digest from the actual dynamics parameters used for the rollout.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n---\n\n### Context\n\n- **PR Author:** @dieterolson\n- **Branch:** `fix/review-feedback-10794-10795`\n- **Reviewed by:** chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\n- **Date:** 2026-09-24T05:03:50Z\n\n---\n\n*This issue was auto-generated from a PR review comment.*"}}}}